course: dictionary
lesson: 12576
title: A formal word for less
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diminution is a long, formal word for a decrease. It means something gets smaller, less, or weaker.
explain: «There was a diminution in rainfall this summer.» Rainfall is how much rain falls, so less rain fell. Test it: «There was a drop in rainfall this summer» still makes sense, so diminution means a decrease.
explain: In everyday talk we say drop, fall or decrease. Diminution is more common in reports, letters and exams. Phrases like «a diminution of» and «without diminution» help you spot it.
fact: Diminution is a noun. It names the act of getting smaller or less.
fact: «Diminution» means a reduction in size, amount, importance or strength.
fact: Diminution is a formal word, so you will meet it more in writing than in chatting.
fact: «Without diminution» means at the same strength or amount all the way through, with no loss.
fact: Decrease, drop and fall are close synonyms, but diminution sounds more formal.
exercise: What does diminution mean? | A new bridge over a river | *A reduction in size or amount | Growing bigger and stronger | A loud noise
exercise: «There was a diminution in rainfall this summer.» What does diminution mean here? | A rainbow | More rain fell | *Less rain fell | A big storm
exercise: The class kept working «without diminution» of effort. What does that mean? | They forgot the task | *They worked just as hard all the way through | They worked less and less | They stopped working halfway
test: Which word means nearly the same as diminution? | Celebration | *Decrease | Whisper | Shine
test: Which sentence shows a diminution? | *The lamp grew dimmer and dimmer | The band played loudly | The cake was baked | The sun rose early
exam: Pick the word that fits: The lake showed a steady ___ in water level over the summer. | rainbow | whisper | celebration | *diminution
